      "side": 1,
      "message": "This solution honestly feels a bit hacky to me and I\u0027m not sure if that\u0027s gonna cause any unintended side effect. I think a better solution would be not passing the file that has diff to the clang format script if the file is considered ignored. But I understand that would take some work to make it happen. I feel like it\u0027s okay to just acknowledge this caveat given that `git cl format` is still doing the right thing. But I\u0027ll stamp the CL and let you decide what\u0027s the best way moving forward given I\u0027m not longer the official owner.",
      "revId": "cdbf20876b2219a72af02a4534e7e56b6c4139a1",
